 Error Handling\n\nPowerShell produces two kinds of errors: **terminating** errors that stop execution, and **non-terminating** errors that report a problem but continue running the next statement. Understanding the difference is essential for writing robust scripts.\n\n## Terminating vs Non-Terminating Errors\n\n- **Non-terminating:** Most cmdlet errors (e.g., `Get-Item` on a file that does not exist). The cmdlet reports the error and moves on.\n- **Terminating:** Errors from the `throw` keyword, .NET exceptions, or cmdlets that encounter critical failures. These stop the current pipeline or script unless caught.\n\n## Controlling Error Behavior\n\nUse `$ErrorActionPreference` to change how non-terminating errors behave for an entire session or script:\n\n```powershell\n$ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"   # Treat all errors as terminating\n```\n\nOr use the `-ErrorAction` parameter on individual cmdlets:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Item \"C:\\nonexistent\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Setting `-ErrorAction Stop` on a cmdlet converts its non-terminating errors into terminating errors, allowing `try/catch` to intercept them.\n\n## try / catch / finally\n\nWrap risky code in a `try` block and handle failures in `catch`. The `finally` block always runs, whether or not an error occurred:\n\n```powershell\ntry {\n    $content = Get-Content \"C:\\data\\config.txt\" -ErrorAction Stop\n    Write-Output \"File loaded successfully.\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Output \"Error: $_\"\n} finally {\n    Write-Output \"Cleanup complete.\"\n}\n```\n\nInside the `catch` block, `$_` (or `$PSItem`) holds the **ErrorRecord** object. You can access details like `$_.Exception.Message` or `$_.ScriptStackTrace`.\n\n## Write-Error vs throw\n\nThese two look similar but behave differently:\n\n```powershell\nWrite-Error \"Something went wrong\"   # Non-terminating by default\nthrow \"Something went wrong\"         # Always terminating\n```\n\n- **`Write-Error`** writes to the error stream but execution continues.\n- **`throw`** immediately stops execution and can be caught by `try/catch`.\n\n> **Key Concept:** Use `throw` when the error is severe enough that the script cannot continue. Use `Write-Error` when you want to report a problem but let the caller decide how to handle it.\n\n## Catching Specific Exceptions\n\nYou can filter `catch` blocks by .NET exception type to handle different errors differently:\n\n```powershell\ntry {\n    $value = [int]\"not_a_number\"\n} catch [System.FormatException] {\n    Write-Output \"Invalid number format.\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Output \"Unexpected error: $_\"\n}\n```\n0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"PowerShell Fundamentals\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/functions-and-parameters\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Functions and Parameters\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[7,\" / \",9]}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/working-with-files\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Working with Files\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Error Handling\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Error Handling\",\"description\":\"Try/catch and ErrorActionPreference.\",\"slug\":\"error-handling\",\"order\":7,\"prerequisites\":[\"m1-l6\"]},\"content\":\"$4\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m1-l7-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a try/catch block that attempts to run Get-Content on a file path stored in $filePath (with -ErrorAction Stop), and in the catch block outputs the error using $_.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with the try keyword followed by a { } block.\",\"Inside try, call Get-Content $filePath -ErrorAction Stop.\",\"Follow with a catch { } block that outputs $_ or uses Write-Output.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"structure\",\"check\":\"has-try-catch\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Your answer needs both a try { } and a catch { } block.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Content\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-Content to read the file.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-ErrorAction\\\\s+Stop\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -ErrorAction Stop so the error becomes terminating.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$_\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use $_ in the catch block to access the error object.\"}],\"solution\":\"try {\\n    Get-Content $filePath -ErrorAction Stop\\n} catch {\\n    Write-Output $_\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"-ErrorAction Stop converts Get-Content's non-terminating error into a terminating error, allowing the catch block to intercept it. $_ holds the ErrorRecord.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l7-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a try/catch/finally block. In the try block, run the command 'Get-Item $path -ErrorAction Stop'. In catch, write 'Error occurred'. In finally, write 'Done'.\",\"hints\":[\"The finally block comes after catch and always runs.\",\"Use Write-Output for each message.\",\"The structure is: try { ... } catch { ... } finally { ... }\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"structure\",\"check\":\"has-try-catch\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include both try and catch blocks.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"finally\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add a finally block after catch.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Item\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-Item in the try block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-ErrorAction\\\\s+Stop\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -ErrorAction Stop to make the error terminating.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Error occurred\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output 'Error occurred' in the catch block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Done\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output 'Done' in the finally block.\"}],\"solution\":\"try {\\n    Get-Item $path -ErrorAction Stop\\n} catch {\\n    Write-Output 'Error occurred'\\n} finally {\\n    Write-Output 'Done'\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The finally block runs regardless of whether an error occurs, making it ideal for cleanup tasks. The -ErrorAction Stop ensures the error is terminating.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l7-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Set the $ErrorActionPreference variable to 'Stop' so that all errors in the script become terminating.\",\"hints\":[\"$$ErrorActionPreference is a preference variable, not a cmdlet.\",\"Assign it a string value.\",\"The value should be 'Stop'.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$ErrorActionPreference\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the $ErrorActionPreference variable.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"=\\\\s*['\\\"]Stop['\\\"]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set the value to 'Stop'.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\",\"explanation\":\"Setting $ErrorActionPreference to 'Stop' converts all non-terminating errors in the current scope into terminating errors, so they can be caught with try/catch.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l7-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a try/catch block that catches only [System.IO.FileNotFoundException]. In the try block, use Get-Content 'missing.txt' -ErrorAction Stop. In catch, output 'File not found'.\",\"hints\":[\"Specify the exception type after the catch keyword in brackets: catch [System.IO.FileNotFoundException].\",\"The exception type goes in square brackets between catch and the opening brace.\",\"Use -ErrorAction Stop on Get-Content to make the error catchable.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"structure\",\"check\":\"has-try-catch\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use a try/catch block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"catch\\\\s*\\\\[System\\\\.IO\\\\.FileNotFoundException\\\\]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Catch the specific [System.IO.FileNotFoundException] type.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Content\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-Content in the try block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"File not found\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output 'File not found' in the catch block.\"}],\"solution\":\"try {\\n    Get-Content 'missing.txt' -ErrorAction Stop\\n} catch [System.IO.FileNotFoundException] {\\n    Write-Output 'File not found'\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"Specifying an exception type in the catch block filters errors — only FileNotFoundException is caught here. Other errors propagate up the call stack.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l7-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a line that uses throw to raise a terminating error with the message 'Configuration file is missing'.\",\"hints\":[\"throw is a keyword, not a cmdlet.\",\"Follow throw with a string message.\",\"This is a single-line statement.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"throw\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the throw keyword.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Configuration file is missing\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include the message 'Configuration file is missing'.\"},{\"rule\":\"forbidden\",\"value\":\"Write-Error\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use throw, not Write-Error — throw creates a terminating error.\"}],\"solution\":\"throw 'Configuration file is missing'\",\"explanation\":\"throw immediately raises a terminating error with the given message. Unlike Write-Error, throw stops execution unless caught by try/catch.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"fundamentals\"}}],\"$L5\"]}],[\"$L6\"],\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\n5:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/functions-and-parameters\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"Functions and Parameters\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/working-with-files\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:tex